      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but i think it's still feeling a bit generic. it reads a little like a standard brochure rather than a hard-hitting proposal that will actually secure funding.\n\nalso, i just ran your draft through our internal screening tool to see where we stand, and the score was actually pretty low. the board is looking for a bit more \"substance\" in terms of the key impact indicators we talked about (the sustainable, empower, transformative, scalable, resilient stuff). \n\ncan you try a second version? i really need you to beef up the impact of those specific concepts so the score is higher, but please—i cannot stress this enough—don't make it look like you're just checking boxes. keep the tone sincere and avoid just listing the words. try to weave them in so naturally that the reader doesn't even realize they're being measured for them. can you make it more punchy and powerful?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
